ere is no declared tool->facade table in the registrar"],"finding":"The plan's core mechanism — 'introspect ... the library facade functions they [MCP tools] wrap' — assumes a derivable tool->facade mapping, but no such declared mapping exists and tool/facade names are not 1:1 (the link_tickets tool wraps rebar.link; edit_ticket wraps rebar.edit_ticket). The facade is invoked as a call inside a decorator-registered closure body, so recovering 'which facade a tool wraps' requires either AST/bytecode analysis of tool bodies or a hand-maintained mapping table — the plan specifies neither, leaving the load-bearing step undefined.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f6affd37cefb50ce4","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach paragraph: 'Introspect the MCP registrar's tool inventory ... and the library facade functions they wrap'","norm_id":"n36269202a7212cfc","priority":0.4288,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer cannot mechanically pair each tool with its facade and either hard-codes a fragile guessed name-equality (misses link->link_tickets) or invents an undocumented mapping mechanism"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"State that the manifest carries an explicit, committed tool->facade name map (seeded once, drift-gated), rather than assuming tool name == facade name.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["1 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Define the library-side comparison signal for **fields-passthrough facades so a declared divergence still catches real MCP-param drift (e.g. record and diff the enumerated MCP param set against an allowlist the facade is known to accept), not just a static 'divergence' flag.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.4973,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["src/rebar/_lib_mutations.py:149 `def edit_ticket(ticket_id: str, *, repo_root=None, **fields)`","src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py:360-372 enumerates title/priority/assignee/.../repos as explicit params","gen_api_surface.py:_params uses inspect.signature — a **fields sink surfaces no per-field descriptor"],"finding":"The plan cites edit_ticket as the known intentional divergence (enumerated MCP params vs **fields passthrough), but the library facade edit_ticket(ticket_id, *, repo_root=None, **fields) 